  E_fit, dR_own, dR_rest, ln_R_fit: the level optimization run with the lines each position claims.  The already known levels are scored against Ritz
  values their own lines helped to place, a position nobody has found against Ritz values placed without it; running the fit removes that asymmetry.
  dR_own is what the position gains once its partners have moved to meet it, dR_rest what the levels the fit moves lose on their own lines, and
  ln_R_fit = ln_R_J + dR_own + dR_rest the change in the total evidence.  A large dR_own with a dR_rest that cancels it is a position the list pays for.
